{"name":"Elastic Pink","hex":"#eca6ca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elastic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Capable of stretching; particularly, capable of stretching so as to return to an original shape or size when force is released.","Made of elastic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elastic material used in clothing, particularly in waistbands and cuffs.","An elastic band."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elastic"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elastic (notion)","blocks":[{"text":"In sewing, elastic is a notion which is sold in narrow strips and generally serves to increase the ability of garment to stretch, either to accommodate movement or to make the garment suitable for wearers of many different physical sizes. Elastic comes in four forms of construction, each with costs and benefits. The component which performs the actual stretching is made of either rubber or a synthetic material such as spandex; this stretching component is then covered with polyester, cotton, nylon, or a combination of these or other fibers which allow it to be attached to clothing. High-quality elastic is able to be stretched to twice its original length and then return to its unflexed state without showing appreciable wear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Corset_%28AM_1996.115.18-1%29.jpg/330px-Corset_%28AM_1996.115.18-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elastic_(notion)","wikidata":"Q10651359"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABurano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_(4531848988)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Jules_Plisson_Stade_francais_2012-03-03.jpg/500px-Jules_Plisson_Stade_francais_2012-03-03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https: